4 \\\\ 2k+1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 2k+1 & 3 & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2k+1 & k \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-4|\\begin{aligned}2k+1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3-0)-(2k+1-k)-4(0-3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-(k+1)-4\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =6-k-1+12 \\\\  & =17-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}17-k & =0 \\\\ k & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k=17.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c97d112-a733-50db-a3e0-14dc2721dcef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $k$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059359} {:answer/id #uuid "a2aa1a94-21f1-552d-ae6c-c5b0802357bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059360} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d37c14-0ed6-5cb1-ae4d-65ca40ec7dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059361} {:answer/id #uuid "0e5ddce2-efab-57ff-834e-5148be9476c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059362} {:answer/id #uuid "73493f5b-e7e5-53c5-91c5-a37d38ea1731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059363}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a3da1235-861c-5299-892e-dbd9ea51bf74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059358}] :question/id #uuid "aae8854c-5bc3-5b0c-a496-72765fde3229" :question/math-academy-id "q-9852" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 & 4k \\\\ 0 & 9 & 5k \\\\ 0 & 11 & 6k\\end{bmatrix}$ is singular."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262917 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fb98df-401c-5fa9-9f2f-08261df60aa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259918} {:answer/id #uuid "220b8b83-724a-5cbe-853b-6caa42638775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260170} {:answer/id #uuid "726ac3fa-740a-5e90-81fa-f599fc3f37a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260875} {:answer/id #uuid "81ca9339-6bce-5219-8fae-787545463a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261005} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6b36bf-bffd-5918-ae53-d958ad6e391a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261101}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81ca9339-6bce-5219-8fae-787545463a11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261005} :answer-field/id #uuid "c45caafc-858f-500e-9ef9-058205b847f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262475}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb6a7e0a-d356-5b58-a703-e0864f9a1a58" :question/math-academy-id "q-128500" :question/problem "Given that\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(B)=12,$ find the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ y & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ y & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ y & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot (1-y)-5\\cdot (2-2y) \\\\  & =12y-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $12,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-12 & =12 \\\\ 12y & =24 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183c086d-012b-5f39-b92e-4550955dfcbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260085} {:answer/id #uuid "2044861f-98f6-51d9-9cf5-e5080be450a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260152} {:answer/id #uuid "21a46985-36f6-5f1d-b213-16f3935ec5b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260165} {:answer/id #uuid "91c5f6e6-19cd-5455-92f6-06f29a9d6687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261142} {:answer/id #uuid "c0800f44-af37-5d5d-b586-92ebc2148392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0800f44-af37-5d5d-b586-92ebc2148392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261575} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a39ba2f-181c-558b-b3c6-6fdf22cdca96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262399}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9517ddd6-18dd-5bea-948b-a75416c96cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-128502" :question/problem "Given that \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ \nand $det(C)=28,$ find the value of $q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & q & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}q & 5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & q \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (q+25)-3\\cdot (-1)+5 \\\\  & =2q+58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $28,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2q+58 & =28 \\\\ 2q & =-30 \\\\ q & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265935 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3472f3af-6fdf-584a-814a-6ecb7e937778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $7$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263460} {:answer/id #uuid "6fe7a9e0-5fc1-5805-b935-6a06de4477cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263966} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f55d58-3424-5ef2-8a1f-da0ba8536bd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264379} {:answer/id #uuid "ac46a045-085c-5912-a741-16ccb2b1102a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $-5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264480} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3d1d69-fac7-5c39-83ff-f1d420f126d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3472f3af-6fdf-584a-814a-6ecb7e937778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $7$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263460} :answer-field/id #uuid "8780a347-d9fa-54e7-9af1-9bb48bd7be2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265483}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50033102-58e0-5acc-81a2-81bf1717d471" :question/math-academy-id "q-130575" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & z \\\\ z & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-48$, find all the possible values of $z.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & z \\\\ z & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}3 & z \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ z & 1\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ z & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3+z)-(2-{z}^{2})+5(-2-3z) \\\\  & =6+2z-2+{z}^{2}-10-15z \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-13z-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-48,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2}-13z-6 & =-48 \\\\ {z}^{2}-13z+42 & =0 \\\\ z & =\\frac{-(-13)\\pm \\sqrt{{13}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 42}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm \\sqrt{1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pm 1}{2} \\\\  & =6,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=6$ and $z=7.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265937 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d38c9cc-ca7f-591e-8a8d-b51db0107fb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263380} {:answer/id #uuid "e51b3361-87bb-58aa-8055-e13c58174671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264992} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c47758-325d-5cfc-acdb-c862f1f74e21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265025} {:answer/id #uuid "ece5b351-94ef-5b84-a4b9-ea4263b1e26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265067} {:answer/id #uuid "f13d3fa2-d171-577a-a448-dd5b107fd44b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ and $-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ece5b351-94ef-5b84-a4b9-ea4263b1e26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-8$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265067} :answer-field/id #uuid "da945efe-22fe-5afe-9a1b-b80334eb4404" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265626}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c642acf-da11-5fe2-a467-6e32aaff486e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130580" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $22$, find all the possible values of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 3 \\\\ 5 & x & 7 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 7 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}5 & x \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(x-14)-2x(5-21)+3(10-3x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-14x+32x+30-9x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+9x+30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $22,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+9x+30 & =22 \\\\ {x}^{2}+9x+8 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{{9}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 8}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9\\pm 7}{2} \\\\  & =-8,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-8$ and $x=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08612547-b005-5392-af1a-df7b474c183f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263076} {:answer/id #uuid "44c75865-eba7-5ea5-899b-6ea970d46b60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263604} {:answer/id #uuid "540dadca-dfc9-5c4a-a4a7-eb33cde6b83b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263725} {:answer/id #uuid "73317ca7-7b96-518c-af47-8c1a296a0e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263999} {:answer/id #uuid "fc9e8555-066d-500b-b643-2c20d52ada5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08612547-b005-5392-af1a-df7b474c183f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263076} :answer-field/id #uuid "f52b9c18-1a55-5825-8634-6431340dd06d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265685}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e9e0a1f-e62f-537b-9ae4-39884aaf945c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130620" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $x$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & -x\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & -x\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ x & -x\\end{aligned}|+8|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-x+2)-5(-x-2x)+8(-1-x) \\\\  & =-3x+6+15x-8-8x \\\\  & =4x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265945 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21390a7b-0a54-5e9a-9011-c7deff139c41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{5}{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263297} {:answer/id #uuid "91d75f72-1a96-5644-a529-caf7355ab1bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264249} {:answer/id #uuid "970c8319-2067-5d80-a590-021621a09030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264292} {:answer/id #uuid "f080186a-d1c4-58fa-9d1f-db014dd38fcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265109} {:answer/id #uuid "fc1c675c-a294-5ee2-a8ca-549d874e48c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-10$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91d75f72-1a96-5644-a529-caf7355ab1bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any value of $p$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264249} :answer-field/id #uuid "a69f31fe-6848-54a7-8e0e-0e1258ee7ad2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265543}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fee93468-4926-51f6-9486-b49c687c7f2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130626" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $p$ given that the matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3p & 4 \\\\ -2 & 6p & -8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3p & 4 \\\\ -2 & 6p & -8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}6p & -8 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3p)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6p \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6p-8)+3p(-2+8)+4(2-6p) \\\\  & =6p-8+18p+8-24p \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, this matrix is singular for all values of $p.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21022c7d-b6d6-5cae-a0a4-a57d89afab0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285086} {:answer/id #uuid "49921218-a78e-55ed-9401-67d5dff3f875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285465} {:answer/id #uuid "5f92b6ee-a669-5379-82fa-e12d81b14834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285665} {:answer/id #uuid "62d465ea-c086-5e0e-baf0-37c50f53cd7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285692} {:answer/id #uuid "b073025c-0c72-5876-88dd-01988080f163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49921218-a78e-55ed-9401-67d5dff3f875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285465} :answer-field/id #uuid "43436436-3068-54a8-97bc-a4c069c2a82c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287296}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa24bddc-180c-5ff0-88bc-f05ee3a66fe1" :question/math-academy-id "q-18252" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $p$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2p-4+10)-0+(-10-6) \\\\  & =2p-4+10-10-6 \\\\  & =2p-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0.$ So,  we have:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p-10 & =0 \\\\ 2p & =10 \\\\ p & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04828dd4-f030-5633-b9ab-2ca90b202225" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284827} {:answer/id #uuid "10872bea-02dc-53b8-8a81-d21f0443ee2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284932} {:answer/id #uuid "28dc2ce6-543c-571a-a921-bb628ebdeb90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285145} {:answer/id #uuid "41f7dafc-fd39-5a57-8833-37de29245686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285398} {:answer/id #uuid "827cdff1-9d64-55e9-b43a-8f9a6a5b14e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41f7dafc-fd39-5a57-8833-37de29245686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285398} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf370fc0-22a1-5807-80d7-314f76c5d442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287538}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "627e7a3d-46e0-5ce8-b4f0-d14bd806cb23" :question/math-academy-id "q-18256" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}]$\n is $81,$ find all the possible values of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ y & -5\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}-3y & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-3y & -2 \\\\ 2 & y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (10-y)-2\\cdot (15y-2)+3\\cdot (-3{y}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =40-4y-30y+4-9{y}^{2}+12 \\\\  & =-9{y}^{2}-34y+56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $81,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{y}^{2}-34y+56 & =81 \\\\ -9{y}^{2}-34y-25 & =0 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+34y+25 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{{34}^{2}-4\\cdot 9\\cdot 25}}{2\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{256}}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm 16}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-17\\pm 8}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $y=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d5ba56-de94-5e4c-b177-c5dc46ffbd51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285000} {:answer/id #uuid "77114028-3901-51ca-9e0e-c825093eb6e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285895} {:answer/id #uuid "7dacdb7f-b468-5607-98ad-e22d7d3b1b14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285945} {:answer/id #uuid "a1c9c2b5-e4ef-5a55-b086-105ff3094bd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286267} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb37ef9-8f27-5f7e-8602-dfc794e1f1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeb37ef9-8f27-5f7e-8602-dfc794e1f1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286978} :answer-field/id #uuid "e17a460e-868e-59c7-9907-c5516e2c691c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287610}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "418920c2-d3a5-5269-af1c-6648eaf6ff36" :question/math-academy-id "q-18271" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-k & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2k & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(A)=-30,$ find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-k & 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2k & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-k|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2k & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2k & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-k\\cdot 3+0-3\\cdot (-6k) \\\\  & =-3k+18k \\\\  & =15k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-30,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15k & =-30 \\\\ k & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121a8609-4bb7-5c67-9bdc-2801df41173e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284949} {:answer/id #uuid "429a9de6-9e34-5d60-bd99-5ca64acccf3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285403} {:answer/id #uuid "77aaca00-7a72-5562-b3c2-49acc2dc1a52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285900} {:answer/id #uuid "a7439201-e9e4-57ad-a8e9-5b2518ed22ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286313} {:answer/id #uuid "c28c20d4-0f99-5907-b488-8276cbb024db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "429a9de6-9e34-5d60-bd99-5ca64acccf3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $5$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285403} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb400fb3-60c2-5a2f-a4e3-20a5f1ab4cc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287536}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a6ffa24-d6e8-52ac-ac3d-5fab4f24df3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-18272" :question/problem "Given that $M=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & p & 0 \\\\ p-3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $det(M)=-23,$ find all the possible values of $p.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & p & 0 \\\\ p-3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}p & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ p-3 & -1\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & p \\\\ p-3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (3p-{p}^{2}) \\\\  & =-3-2{p}^{2}+6p \\\\  & =-2{p}^{2}+6p-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-23,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{p}^{2}+6p-3 & =-23 \\\\ 2{p}^{2}-6p-20 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-3p-10 & =0 \\\\ p & =\\frac{-(-3)\\pm \\sqrt{(-3)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot (-10)}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pm 7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions are $p=-2$ and $p=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295140 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b6fb57b-36e2-543a-ab01-e63593d507d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b6fb57b-36e2-543a-ab01-e63593d507d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293544} :answer-field/id #uuid "9633885c-c66b-52e8-84a6-2cf06bb918b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294471}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8c1908a-4170-5ad4-8920-81bd7dfc6050" :question/math-academy-id "q-280403" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $det(A)=37$, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(F) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}x & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}3 & x \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(x\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 5)-(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2(x-20)-(3+8) \\\\  & =2x-40-11 \\\\  & =2x-51\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $37,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-51 & =37 \\\\ 2x & =88 \\\\ x & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd58d80d-e3cd-55e9-ab3a-7f344ff3bcd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd58d80d-e3cd-55e9-ab3a-7f344ff3bcd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293792} :answer-field/id #uuid "de3f45f5-c264-5c0e-b8b4-960fb94c3f56" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294706}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b09153b7-90f9-5996-a92d-2d17cff9a754" :question/math-academy-id "q-280404" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}k+1 & 2k & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & k & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is singular.\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det & =|\\begin{aligned}k+1 & 2k & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & k & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(k+1)|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ k & 1\\end{aligned}|-2k|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(k+1)(5\\cdot 1-0\\cdot k)-2k(0\\cdot 1-0\\cdot -2)+3(0\\cdot k-5\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =(k+1)(5)-2k(0)+3(10) \\\\  & =5k+5+30 \\\\  & =5k+35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5k+35 & =0 \\\\ 5k & =-35 \\\\ k & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4fa7fe2-70f7-5b48-aad2-0f11a308a02b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4fa7fe2-70f7-5b48-aad2-0f11a308a02b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293639} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff1893bf-705b-5320-b68c-49a5e5fad6f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294826}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cae37ba1-c114-55f8-b121-0094f150645e" :question/math-academy-id "q-280519" :question/problem "Given that $G=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x-1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}]$ is singular, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x-1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ x+1 & -4\\end{aligned}|-(2x-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & x+1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(3\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot (x+1))-(2x-1)(0)+6(0\\cdot (x+1)-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =x(-12)+0+6(3) \\\\  & =-12x+18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12x+18 & =0 \\\\ -12x & =-18 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7a14d7c-c976-5346-a0ff-1a7451eb909b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7a14d7c-c976-5346-a0ff-1a7451eb909b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293594} :answer-field/id #uuid "744d1c09-7fab-597a-b711-9626275fab38" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294339} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e75f6dd-e85a-5f64-bcc4-624a0a4629af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e75f6dd-e85a-5f64-bcc4-624a0a4629af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292998} :answer-field/id #uuid "d728a0ab-06b9-5153-aa9d-039b19b0b1ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294689}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "854d343a-6ceb-5dbc-aed9-5a3bba384840" :question/math-academy-id "q-280540" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of $[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]$ is $32$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ x & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}x & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|+0 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(-2\\cdot 0-(-1)(4))-3(x\\cdot 0-(-1)(1)) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)(4)-3(1) \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-8-3 \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $32$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-11 & =32 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =43 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{43}{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{43}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}$ and $x=\\frac{\\sqrt{43}}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0455064-a7d8-59fd-ac77-33abf41ca336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293865}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0455064-a7d8-59fd-ac77-33abf41ca336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293865} :answer-field/id #uuid "718e1993-6243-5b67-ad85-b48d5e4c1b0e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5474c54-161f-5c59-93d2-847eb2a1ab3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5474c54-161f-5c59-93d2-847eb2a1ab3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293891} :answer-field/id #uuid "904e7486-ae2f-53e2-a8b8-33a2fef9eb06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294451}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f11851f4-08f0-546e-8ec7-83f1d8f0d049" :question/math-academy-id "q-280541" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of $[\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ is $40$, find all the possible values of $x$ **in ascending order**.\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Let’s use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 2x & 5 \\\\ 3 & x & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x|\\begin{aligned}x & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}3 & x \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x(2x-4)-2x(3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 7)+5(3-7x) \\\\  & =x(2x-4)-2x(-22)+15-35x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-4x+44x+15-35x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}+5x+15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $40$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5x+15 & =40 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+5x-25 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5\\pm \\sqrt{{5}^{2}-4(2)(-25)}}{2(2)} \\\\ x & =\\frac{-5+\\sqrt{225}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-5\\pm 15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, **in ascending order**, the solutions are $x=-5$ and $x=\\frac{5}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24569432-1366-5b0e-a6fa-35329602b43d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360990} {:answer/id #uuid "405ba37d-88bc-588c-be97-45c88986f4c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361126} {:answer/id #uuid "822d6e62-ce1f-5081-8c99-18fcb72e9a13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361416} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0b9dec-a477-56d5-8568-22939d39be14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ and $-3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361539} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c897ad-8b3e-52b7-83a5-70beda9d09d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361665}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24569432-1366-5b0e-a6fa-35329602b43d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360990} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fe2b409-187a-57b6-9b05-5d49a74a922b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362129}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e554c090-e3bc-5a93-90b4-9f79a0997b62" :question/math-academy-id "q-9911" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & k \\\\ 1 & k & -k \\\\ 5 & k & k\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & k \\\\ 1 & k & -k \\\\ 5 & k & k\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}k & -k \\\\ k & k\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -k \\\\ 5 & k\\end{aligned}|+k|\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ 5 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({k}^{2}+{k}^{2})+(k+5k)+k(k-5k) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k+k\\cdot (-4k) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k-4{k}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{k}^{2}+6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{k}^{2}+6k & =0 \\\\ k(-2k+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=0$ and $k=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362379 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28576cc0-5b53-52a1-993c-52e6981f0e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361011} {:answer/id #uuid "41df7ae9-3272-5a1d-b2c6-8730c296899a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Any real number" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361129} {:answer/id #uuid "a0b997e7-f26c-5ca5-b635-2f16f0cab1c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361556} {:answer/id #uuid "a555d756-093c-5a66-ac31-9396b628afff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361577} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a9bece-ac6f-57f6-abed-e01a47669f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0b997e7-f26c-5ca5-b635-2f16f0cab1c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361556} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3d836f-c871-5036-ada8-8e641e2d9862" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362089}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec95474f-3d89-5428-8221-da33b63b3f3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9961" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}1 & n & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ is $-6$, find the value of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & n & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4-n\\cdot 2+0 \\\\  & =4-2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-6,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-2n & =-6 \\\\ -2n & =-10 \\\\ n & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365547 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40e1e46e-bc20-5e49-8f3c-e2b13ee9e67f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{67}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40e1e46e-bc20-5e49-8f3c-e2b13ee9e67f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{67}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365549} :answer-field/id #uuid "20261a72-2d87-53f3-be96-928a95530e46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365548}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbb701de-fecd-5033-b2e0-5f19c68c7b4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280402" :question/problem "Given that $B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & k+2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $det(B)=70$, find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & k+2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3|\\begin{aligned}k+2 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & k+2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(6\\cdot (k+2)-(-5)(-1))+2(1\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (k+2)) \\\\  & =3(6k+12-5)+2(-1-4k-8) \\\\  & =3(6k+7)+2(-4k-9) \\\\  & =18k+21-8k-18 \\\\  & =10k+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $70,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10k+3 & =70 \\\\ 10k & =67 \\\\ k & =\\frac{67}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e337463-b3e6-57c5-a2b0-3b2f8be1327c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e337463-b3e6-57c5-a2b0-3b2f8be1327c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365552} :answer-field/id #uuid "113f8edf-ce63-5e3c-8e20-25df8fcc000b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365551} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5aa7c3b-3cc6-5915-9f4e-4ad87619a68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5aa7c3b-3cc6-5915-9f4e-4ad87619a68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365554} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae0cbef-0d94-5f00-b36b-22a479b003a4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365553}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7046d61a-2100-5f6e-80e3-9459516462dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-280543" :question/problem "Find, in **ascending order**, the values ​​of $x$ for which the following matrix is singular.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x+2 & 2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & x & x+1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn ascending order, $x=$\n{{field-1}} and $x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}x+2 & 2x & 4 \\\\ 3 & x & x+1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =(x+2)|\\begin{aligned}x & x+1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2x|\\begin{aligned}3 & x+1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}3 & x \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(x+2)(3x)-2x(8-x)+4(-x) \\\\  & =3x(x+2)-2x(8-x)-4x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+6x-16x+2{x}^{2}-4x \\\\  & =5{x}^{2}-14x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-14x & =0 \\\\ x(5x-14) & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\,\\text{or}\\,x=\\frac{14}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{14}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396237 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48ffa317-1b68-57e4-8682-58b3f2cf3610" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396239} {:answer/id #uuid "43dbf530-ae59-578a-b191-6ba7d2edf47b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396240} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c887a0-8c33-5ac9-b8f5-287ee0622dd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ and $0$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396241} {:answer/id #uuid "0a134bc9-3211-56a8-ba64-b5d8b1f67691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ and $2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396242} {:answer/id #uuid "c63b5ccb-5750-5b73-bc77-0f7d019725ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a134bc9-3211-56a8-ba64-b5d8b1f67691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0$ and $2$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396242} :answer-field/id #uuid "0631763f-bf07-54e2-9810-4d0b16208a88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396238}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11af43ea-89bf-58ea-b458-4433226aa764" :question/math-academy-id "q-9913" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix  $[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}k & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k\\end{aligned}| & =k|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(3k-6)+0+0 \\\\  & =k(3k-6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0.$ So,  we have:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(3k-6) & =0 \\\\ 3k(k-2) & =0 \\\\ k & =0,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=0$ and $k=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d167c86-2957-5856-9829-ed639fe987fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400368} {:answer/id #uuid "f4b0080f-3903-56c0-99e9-1c714284d709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400369} {:answer/id #uuid "7b00f40d-f528-5d51-ba17-148c04c5be0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-5$ and $1$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400370} {:answer/id #uuid "dc29467d-2e6d-5f49-8946-656bd765b95a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400371} {:answer/id #uuid "0545f2be-36f5-50f6-a5cb-3ece6041700e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ and $3$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4b0080f-3903-56c0-99e9-1c714284d709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $8$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400369} :answer-field/id #uuid "53dd3293-7046-5b2d-b374-9c7bbea414c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400367}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "30a80f14-b653-5ec9-a12d-20d43bb40f91" :question/math-academy-id "q-128506" :question/problem "Given that the determinant of\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nis $-29$, find all the possible values of $m.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $m:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & m \\\\ m & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-6|\\begin{aligned}m & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+m|\\begin{aligned}m & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-0)-6(m-0)+m(m-6) \\\\  & =3-6m+{m}^{2}-6m \\\\  & ={m}^{2}-12m+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-29,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-12m+3 & =-29 \\\\ {m}^{2}-12m+32 & =0 \\\\ m & =\\frac{-(-12)\\pm \\sqrt{{12}^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 32}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\pm 4}{2} \\\\  & =6\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $m=4$ and $m=8.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064152 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064035 :question/id #uuid "b7051104-6e23-5ab2-8779-5d54a3c3f5f5" :question/math-academy-id "e-270" :question/problem "Consider a spherical balloon with radius $r.$ As the balloon loses air, its volume $V$ decreases. What is the best interpretation of $V'(r)?$\n\n![](images/7f/7f52288ca4670375413ecd5283bc2d15fbb332af311ead07986c1526d25e338a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The function $V(r)$ gives the volume of a sphere with radius $r.$ So\n\n$$\nV'(r) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}V}{\\textrm{d}r} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{Change in }V}{\\textrm{Change in }r}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $V'(r)$ is the rate at which the volume changes as the radius changes."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "159b4d58-b34d-52cd-aad2-2c058f772ad2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049362 :topic/math-academy-id 337 :topic/title "The Instantaneous Rate of Change of a Function at a Point"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ec57e68-f96f-5b48-b52c-8b36af1420aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The area of a circle with radius $r$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063044} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2f68c6-cc44-5265-950e-997a1aa2ad3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the radius changes as the area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063045} {:answer/id #uuid "f2762674-a011-5f07-98aa-edaec50b70d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The length of the radius of the circle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063046} {:answer/id #uuid "0dc27870-8a25-53e7-873e-b2b72c41ee2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circumference of the circle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063047} {:answer/id #uuid "2552a089-758a-50be-bdb2-e768280d5b71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the radius changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063048}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4dcbc737-4a4b-57d7-acdf-f517b5036115" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063043}] :question/id #uuid "898560df-2720-5fc0-88be-08678b6642b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-48616" :question/problem "Consider a circle such that the radius $r$ can vary. If $A$ is the area of the circle, what is the best interpretation of $A^{′}(r)$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21259e1a-7c04-5c09-82e5-7243bcf85664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The area of a rectangle with base $b$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327218} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc94605-ed86-5627-829b-c4455291deab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the height changes as the area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327776} {:answer/id #uuid "65f9a132-8f61-5572-a179-107ef44e827e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The length of the base of the rectangle" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327819} {:answer/id #uuid "a66e4302-c64c-5bcf-b355-707357f1f6a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the height changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328373} {:answer/id #uuid "fe57e3fa-21c0-5395-89e5-133cd34e4d57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the base changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe57e3fa-21c0-5395-89e5-133cd34e4d57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the base changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329169} :answer-field/id #uuid "17ac5fb5-0106-5c51-8d69-9c1dee49bf09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329225}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3408555-de68-5409-ab55-f212404a9d43" :question/math-academy-id "q-48684" :question/problem "Consider a rectangle such that the height is fixed but its base $b$ can vary. What is the best interpretation of ${A}^{′}(b)$ if $A$ is the area of the rectangle?" :question/worked-solution "The function $A(b)$ gives the area of a rectangle with base $b.$ So\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(b)=\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}b}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }A}{\\text{Change in }b}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${A}^{′}(b)$ is the rate at which the area changes as the base changes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0481bb38-274e-5774-875a-be793cabede3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the major axis changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244351} {:answer/id #uuid "6f685a56-5b54-54ac-9038-c2f2549391ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The major axis of an ellipse with area S" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245305} {:answer/id #uuid "8b1e11b2-d40a-56e1-ae24-9b4be247f86b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the perimeter changes as the major axis changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245533} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a35ba0-4aeb-5454-978c-23ba5d8750bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the major axis changes as the minor axis changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246336} {:answer/id #uuid "ea4062cd-2591-577d-8695-888b8ea68b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The area of an ellipse with major axis $a$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0481bb38-274e-5774-875a-be793cabede3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as the major axis changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244351} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d129f8a-681e-53f4-b910-966663b5b595" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246792}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "45b2e799-d000-5801-973f-7fb80701d236" :question/math-academy-id "q-112063" :question/problem "Consider an ellipse such that its major axis $a$ can vary while its minor axis is fixed. What is the best interpretation of ${S}^{′}(a)$ if $S$ is the area enclosed by the ellipse?" :question/worked-solution "The function $S(a)$ gives the area of the ellipse with major axis $a.$ So,\n\n$$\n{S}^{′}(a)=\\frac{\\text{d}S}{\\text{d}a}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }S}{\\text{Change in }a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${S}^{′}(a)$ is the rate at which the area changes as the major axis changes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a3c608b-0776-5682-807c-c217199505fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The length of each side of the cube" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327849} {:answer/id #uuid "821f7ab3-b9fa-5e2e-874b-4fb96cb126a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which each side changes as the volume changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328056} {:answer/id #uuid "a04c5fbf-fabc-5b22-b73b-1f7f7eb0701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the volume changes as each side changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328321} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c51007-5a0a-5a87-9323-57b4562c0a35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The volume of a cube with side $s$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328826} {:answer/id #uuid "f87b7a58-612c-5146-a7cc-b44d08303d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the surface area of the cube changes as each side changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a04c5fbf-fabc-5b22-b73b-1f7f7eb0701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the volume changes as each side changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328321} :answer-field/id #uuid "3038a62b-8e82-50ea-b5ff-048978515d05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329272}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2649901e-51a7-5a33-8419-dccdedf85db4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48685" :question/problem "Consider a cube such that the length of each side $s$ varies. What is the best interpretation of ${V}^{′}(s)$ if $V$ is the volume of the cube?" :question/worked-solution "The function $V(s)$ gives the volume of a cube with side $s.$ So,\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }V}{\\text{Change in }s}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${V}^{′}(s)$ is the rate at which the volume changes as each side changes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00b82256-6880-5f2d-9892-6174ae0f0d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which each side changes as the area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326943} {:answer/id #uuid "094a2cc0-b936-5de6-8065-8d9a6b12b18a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The length of each side of the square" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327008} {:answer/id #uuid "4f1aefff-cc0b-5ea7-aa13-a53ad2b5454e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which each side of the square changes as the perimeter changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327621} {:answer/id #uuid "a6805a91-c909-5b04-9593-096bb078287f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as each side changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328375} {:answer/id #uuid "b813c83e-8dc3-5bee-af28-10168270e41a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The area of a square with side $s$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00b82256-6880-5f2d-9892-6174ae0f0d0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which each side changes as the area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326943} :answer-field/id #uuid "2092f13c-e49b-57f7-9c52-1f0a1e28d77d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329240}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7fb93d4f-f465-58a7-ac76-ee7ee1e78375" :question/math-academy-id "q-48686" :question/problem "Consider a square such that its area $A$ can vary. What is the best interpretation of ${s}^{′}(A)$ if $s$ is the length of each side of the square?" :question/worked-solution "The function $s(A)$ gives the length of each side of a square with area $A.$ So,\n\n$$\n{s}^{′}(A)=\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}A}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }s}{\\text{Change in }A}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${s}^{′}(A)$ is the rate at which each side changes as the area changes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d85ca26-875b-529b-bb07-e98e43e92c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the volume changes as the surface area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336306} {:answer/id #uuid "304e3f79-8da4-5722-864b-6e088ffb40b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the volume changes as the radius changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336496} {:answer/id #uuid "7a2466a3-db1c-58e7-b6a8-52c297f1b61a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the surface area changes as the radius changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337131} {:answer/id #uuid "a4fb944c-c55d-5347-b4f6-7c78b85fb0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the radius changes as the volume changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337532} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d3818b-f99d-5a24-b5f8-6df2128b8b17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the radius changes as the surface area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4fb944c-c55d-5347-b4f6-7c78b85fb0b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the radius changes as the volume changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337532} :answer-field/id #uuid "b62051ba-1ffa-5ae8-a7ea-8260e883f62d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338610}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5325b1f7-e675-515b-98cd-c46e0c3ccc93" :question/math-academy-id "q-72099" :question/problem "Consider a sphere such that its volume $V$ can vary. What is the best interpretation of ${r}^{′}(V)$ if $r$ is the length of the radius of the sphere?" :question/worked-solution "The function $r(V)$ gives the length of the radius of a sphere with volume $V.$ So,\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(V)=\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}V}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }r}{\\text{Change in }V}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${r}^{′}(V)$ is the rate at which the radius changes as the volume changes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f73173-53b3-594c-9f00-73f6211f3aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the perimeter changes as each side changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336106} {:answer/id #uuid "2f86ab33-c24f-513c-9f78-18726fd0321b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the area changes as each side changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336488} {:answer/id #uuid "8526b1a3-6e9c-580f-9c0b-82c5736c43b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which each side changes as the perimeter changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337231} {:answer/id #uuid "95ba1001-8463-59e2-bed5-38495c9afaab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the perimeter changes as the area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337400} {:answer/id #uuid "eddb83ed-12b2-59b9-8dd1-0e4ed245941a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which each side changes as the area changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08f73173-53b3-594c-9f00-73f6211f3aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The rate at which the perimeter changes as each side changes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336106} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa385052-bba0-5f25-abff-7baf2aaa746f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338590}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c47d8541-4bf8-5eff-901b-cba03fe2cd37" :question/math-academy-id "q-72104" :question/problem "Consider a regular pentagon such that the length $s$ of each side varies. What is the best interpretation of ${P}^{′}(s)$ if $P$ is the perimeter of the pentagon?" :question/worked-solution "The function $P(s)$ gives the perimeter of a pentagon with side $s.$ So,\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}P}{\\text{d}s}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }P}{\\text{Change in }s}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${P}^{′}(s)$ is the rate at which the perimeter changes as each side changes."}] :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Derivative of a Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064153 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064036 :question/id #uuid "8378ead2-9247-55a0-acc8-2e6d0874ea09" :question/math-academy-id "e-271" :question/problem "The function $B(s)$ models a school's budget, in dollars, given the average number of students $s$ in each grade. What is the best interpretation of $B'(30)=2\\,000?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $B'(s)$ represents the rate at which the budget is changing at the moment when the school has an average of exactly $s$ students in each grade.\n\nTherefore, $B'(30) = 2\\,000$ means:\n\n*When the school has an average of $30$ students in each grade, its budget is increasing at a rate of $2\\,000$ dollars per student.*"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2451a654-2255-5867-871d-54340dfeff81" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6b77c5-ddfd-5b08-a361-9ab4187a9d4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users increased at a rate of $650$ users per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327481} {:answer/id #uuid "80be97f8-97ac-5b85-a8f9-3150ff9145c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of users increased at a constant rate of $162.5$ users per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328044} {:answer/id #uuid "9ebe19ed-4105-5740-8271-2100f1c58c04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, there are exactly $650$ users." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328304} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3d8b40-f651-514c-8adb-8e02d8ddf76f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users decreased at a rate of $650$ users per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328581} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ba5d88-2149-5501-afd7-d16c293347cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The number of users increased by $650$ during the first $4$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e6b77c5-ddfd-5b08-a361-9ab4187a9d4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users increased at a rate of $650$ users per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327481} :answer-field/id #uuid "6590d944-81ce-5446-a022-cd1f094cac01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329364}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b66dae7-140e-5116-ac81-188561d113a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-48571" :question/problem "The function $U(t)$ models the number of users of a new mobile phone app, $t$ hours after launching the app. What is the best interpretation of ${U}^{′}(4)=650?$" :question/worked-solution "The function ${U}^{′}(t)$ represents the rate at which the number of users is changing at the moment $t$ hours after launch. \n\nTherefore, ${U}^{′}(4)=650$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users increased at a rate of $650$ users per hour*"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9147ca2b-21f1-5de4-b4c7-0232f2bf011d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ days after taking up walking, the distance Sam walked increased at a constant rate of $40$ meters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063038} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e020b6-134e-573d-84c7-782bc75c5d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ days after taking up walking, the distance Sam walked decreased at a rate of $120$ meters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063039} {:answer/id #uuid "207c47ee-9408-5a08-a5cc-7712df25cafe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ days after taking up walking, the distance Sam walked increased at a rate of $120$ meters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063040} {:answer/id #uuid "2a149e5c-32d5-5b80-9960-b0fde15c7543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The distance Sam walked increased by $120$ meters after $3$ days" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063041} {:answer/id #uuid "42d69a74-83a5-55c2-98ac-a586ed0a850c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Sam walked a distance of $120m$ on day $3$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063042}] :answer-field/id #uuid "45e8b60d-d769-561c-b6bd-4b1f7461d04b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063037}] :question/id #uuid "4e1cc79f-955c-55ff-8a45-431467ad302e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48615" :question/problem "Sam decides to take up walking. The function $W(d)$ models the number of meters Sam walks on day $d$. What is the best interpretation of $W^{′}(3) = 120$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18483a9d-19e4-5f94-b2a3-ccccfd7f979e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet is $7$ squared centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244531} {:answer/id #uuid "4b863b01-cf1b-55e4-8e69-ced74eb63dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet decreases at a rate of $7$ squared centimeters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244987} {:answer/id #uuid "7207d4d5-bdb8-5ca0-a328-3e372f8a84b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ minutes after the observation began, the area of the sheet increases at a rate of $5$ squared centimeters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245330} {:answer/id #uuid "c5223869-c963-538b-9410-367ef3c5275a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "During the first $5$ minutes of the observations, the area has constantly decreased at a rate of $7$ squared centimeters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246064} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e741b1-353c-521e-82dd-ff9e63e5f868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet is $5$ squared centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b863b01-cf1b-55e4-8e69-ced74eb63dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet decreases at a rate of $7$ squared centimeters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244987} :answer-field/id #uuid "56fc86c1-4956-5dcf-b00f-3efb286cbbe4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246700}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "152b8d9d-0ba8-513e-8b4b-b5c65402cd59" :question/math-academy-id "q-112091" :question/problem "The function $S(t)$ gives the area, in squared centimeters, of a thin sheet of ice as it melts $t$ minutes after observations start. What is the best interpretation of ${S}^{′}(5)=-7?$" :question/worked-solution "The function ${S}^{′}(t)$ represents the rate at which the area of the sheet is decreasing $t$ minutes after the beginning of the observation.\n\nTherefore, since it is negative, ${S}^{′}(5)=-7$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$5$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet decreases at a rate of $7$ squared centimeters per minute.*"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329907 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be07498-8050-537a-b25e-fd95bab4699a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The distance traveled increased by $10$ meters during the first $30$ seconds" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327037} {:answer/id #uuid "51437d5b-5e6c-5066-b244-e7e818095097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The distance traveled increased at a constant rate of $3$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327641} {:answer/id #uuid "7aadd70b-53c1-50fb-bc02-b723b6f3ea3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled decreased at a rate of $10$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327987} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa8d265-16ad-5285-82fb-8aa43f6dd27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the car traveled $10$ meters." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328410} {:answer/id #uuid "dc11c238-8417-5632-881c-cdb922cfb484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled increased at a rate of $10$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc11c238-8417-5632-881c-cdb922cfb484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled increased at a rate of $10$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328858} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffcaa0c5-cbb7-57a1-b1e2-92acc3accb1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329631}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce5be28b-4511-5653-9464-457a2f9e4167" :question/math-academy-id "q-48688" :question/problem "The function $x(t)$ models the number of meters traveled by a car, $t$ seconds after it sets off on a journey. What is the best interpretation of ${x}^{′}(30)=10?$" :question/worked-solution "The function ${x}^{′}(t)$ represents the rate at which the number of meters is changing at the moment $t$ seconds after starting its journey.\n\nTherefore, ${x}^{′}(30)=10$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$30$ seconds after the start of the journey, the distance traveled increased at a rate of $10$ meters per second*"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5311f292-28d9-536c-a8d6-76f581020fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "When $4$ liters of lemonade are sold the previous day, the price increases at a rate of $50$ cents per liter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327656} {:answer/id #uuid "5b26485f-079b-5131-9807-49132e36cd1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "When the price of lemonade equals $50$ cents, the amount sold decreases at a rate of $4$ liters per dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327733} {:answer/id #uuid "8289da38-36b9-5f3c-87a1-9de5ef9ae635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "When $4$ liters of lemonade are sold the previous day, the price decreases at a rate of $50$ cents per liter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328058} {:answer/id #uuid "c8964a2d-05f1-54d8-9be3-654b70a801b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "When $4$ liters of lemonade were sold the previous day, the price of lemonade is equal to $50$ cents." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328696} {:answer/id #uuid "e62a5970-e183-506c-bd95-1967e4afdccd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "When the price of lemonade equals $50$ cents, the amount sold increases at a rate of $4$ liters per dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5311f292-28d9-536c-a8d6-76f581020fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "When $4$ liters of lemonade are sold the previous day, the price increases at a rate of $50$ cents per liter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327656} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f0c3d8e-fad5-500b-885a-e1b994af0177" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329308}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "682e5334-b209-5f44-9ceb-8ea5b223ef4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-48691" :question/problem "The function $P(v)$ models the price of lemonade sold at a lemonade stand, in dollars, depending on the volume $v$ sold the previous day, in liters. What is the best interpretation of the statement below?\n\n$\\,$ *The slope of the tangent line to the graph of $P(v)$ at $v=4$ is equal to $0.5.$*" :question/worked-solution "The slope of the line tangent to the graph of $P(v)$ at $v=4$ gives the derivative of $P(v)$ at $v=4.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(4)=0.5.\n$$\n\nWe can interpret the above statement as\n\n$\\,$ *When $4$ liters of lemonade are sold the previous day, the price is increasing at a rate of $50$ cents per liter.*"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329911 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "224a9606-2cff-583a-a5a5-2ad7bd61c0d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ hours after launching, the number of visitors decreased at a rate of $1\\,500$ visitors per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327231} {:answer/id #uuid "2805d6d9-2178-5b35-a75a-b51a961ecf7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ hours after launching, the number of visitors increased by a total of $1\\,500$ visitors" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327275} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5469b6-041f-5e92-a4a1-d055f18d58b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ hours after launching, the number of visitors increased at a rate of $1\\,500$ visitors per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327334} {:answer/id #uuid "63be821f-e737-542f-b20e-fcd904ca356a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ hours after launching, the number of visitors increased at a constant rate of $150$ visitors per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327801} {:answer/id #uuid "9571fdf5-f5e6-5c7d-844e-6c82e23412aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ hours after launching, the number of visitors decreased by a total of $1\\,500$ visitors" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d5469b6-041f-5e92-a4a1-d055f18d58b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ hours after launching, the number of visitors increased at a rate of $1\\,500$ visitors per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327334} :answer-field/id #uuid "b67658e3-d1f9-53fe-9d3e-ca9f1907b2b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329503}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d89bcd84-b867-5262-b6e7-a8266afa7fe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-48709" :question/problem "The function $V(t)$ models the number of visitors, in thousands, to a new website, $t$ hours after the website's launch. What is the best interpretation of the statement below?\n\n$\\,$ *The slope of the tangent line to the graph of $V(t)$ at $t=10$ is equal to $1.5.$*" :question/worked-solution "The slope of the line tangent to the graph of $V(t)$ at $t=10$ gives the derivative of $V(t)$ at $t=10.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(10)=1.5.\n$$\n\nWe can interpret the above statement as\n\n$\\,$ *$10$ hours after launching, the number of visitors increased at a rate of $1\\,500$ visitors per hour.*"}] :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Derivative of a Function in a Given Context"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064154 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064037 :question/id #uuid "750e7350-1434-56ef-80d8-7cf531108f96" :question/math-academy-id "e-273" :question/problem "On a particular day, the rate $E$ at which tourists enter a small country can be modeled as $E(t) = 50\\cdot 3^{0.2t}$ tourists per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, after midnight. The rate at which tourists leave the country can be modeled as $L(t)=100\\cdot 2^{0.2t}$ tourists per hour, where $t$ is also the time in hours after midnight.\n\nWhat is the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}?$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the number of tourists in the country at time $t$ is equal to the entry rate minus the exit rate at time $t,$ that is, \n\n$$\nE(t)-L(t).\n$$\n\nSince $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is ten hours after midnight, we have $t=10.$ Substituting $t=10,$ the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E(10)-L(10) & =50\\cdot {3}^{0.2(10)}-100\\cdot {2}^{0.2(10)} \\\\  & =450-400 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the number of tourists in the country at $10\\text{:}00\\,\\textrm{am}$ is $50$ tourists per hour."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7df31c9-b27a-5ce2-93c8-178ba96da000" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064839 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0471e9db-ae74-5721-881f-6766ec471aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$55$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063092} {:answer/id #uuid "0cb451c9-624d-5aea-a847-0a716186f298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063093} {:answer/id #uuid "19b1cbfa-5dc1-50c7-b795-45e8078bcfc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063094} {:answer/id #uuid "1b66f55e-690d-507d-9f15-da5db4e9d4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$77$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063095} {:answer/id #uuid "20cf6a46-231f-5311-8a1f-d91f99078953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$66$ crocodiles per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063096}] :answer-field/id #uuid "68d15ded-f5ea-533d-bc58-1b30eba5bad8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063091}] :question/id #uuid "7cc5ee70-2b10-5325-a2dc-cd7c11e6d8be" :question/math-academy-id "q-48935" :question/problem "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t) = 6 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t) = 4 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000$.\n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2012$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82402f4c-fc78-5115-abbb-8ad3dc43491f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063098} {:answer/id #uuid "cc715b82-ec3a-5165-93b6-be32e1b392a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1.4$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063099} {:answer/id #uuid "fab10240-8482-561c-8059-251f3e1c7340" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ liter per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063100} {:answer/id #uuid "47d9e4ac-1056-5034-b06d-e6db26008fa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063101} {:answer/id #uuid "6c4a5028-9eb2-5a86-a7ba-fc7fb96b071f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1.5$ liters per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063102}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e37c85c4-0030-5b58-beda-4e374bfaab62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063097}] :question/id #uuid "d91740bb-0717-56e4-8960-7951b9ef1956" :question/math-academy-id "q-48936" :question/problem "The rate $F$ at which a swimming pool is being filled can be modeled as $F(t) = t^{2} - t$ liters per minute, where $t$ is the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled. The rate at which water is leaking from the pool can be modeled as $L(t) = \\frac{1}{4}t^{2}$ liters per minute, where $t$ is also the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled.\n\nWhat is the rate of change of the volume of water in the pool $2$ minutes after the pool began to be filled?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233148 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04af5409-c23e-5a9b-9822-6f64b5d41018" :question/math-academy-id "q-112382" :question/problem "After taking a pill containing $300$ milligrams of a particular drug, the quantity of the drug in a patient's body decreases at a rate of $c(t)=300\\cdot {2}^{-0.7t}$ milligrams per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the patient consumed the pill. What will be the rate of decrease after $5$ hours? Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the quantity of the drug in the patient's body after $5$ hours, we have $t=5.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease in the quantity of the drug after $5$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(5) & =300\\cdot {2}^{-0.7(5)} \\\\  & =300\\cdot {2}^{-3.5} \\\\  & \\approx 27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $27$ milligrams per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b018299-7007-54eb-bc89-99c9efa7a6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b018299-7007-54eb-bc89-99c9efa7a6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232200} :answer-field/id #uuid "60e7eb70-1c1f-5c79-88b8-72f4909c2ea9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232199}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d565b38-f76f-5424-8185-fe15e9499b1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142994" :question/problem "What was the exact rate of change of the stock's value at week $9?$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ thousand dollars per week." :question/worked-solution "The function ${h}^{'}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the stock, applicable in the domain of $h(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the stock at $x=9$ weeks is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{'}(9) & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the stock price was $\\frac{1}{9}$ thousand dollars per week."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234095 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e0f698f-6d3a-555d-aa86-2a4465688985" :question/math-academy-id "q-48608" :question/problem "The birth rate of a krill population is modeled by $B(t)=5\\cdot {2}^{0.7t}$ thousands of tons per year, where $t$ is the time, in years, since $1998.$ What was the birth rate, in thousands of tons per year, for the krill in $2008?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $B(t)$ models the birth rate for the krill, in thousands of tons, $t$ years since $1998.$ Since we want the birth rate in $2008$, then $t=10$ years.\n\nThus, the birth rate for the krill in $2008$ was\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(10) & =5\\cdot {2}^{0.7(10)} \\\\  & =5\\cdot {2}^{7} \\\\  & =640.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the birth rate for the krill in $2008$ was $640$ thousand tons per year."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae60046d-e068-5985-a664-cad5d031ad4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae60046d-e068-5985-a664-cad5d031ad4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1/2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234812} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9203a5f-745f-5240-bf02-625bcda44d5b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235251}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0e7cbce-5689-5b4d-bba5-cc1bd41aa26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-167562" :question/problem "What was the exact rate of change of the stock's value at week $4?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$ thousand dollars per week." :question/worked-solution "The function ${g}^{′}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the stock, applicable in the domain of $g(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the stock at $x=4$ weeks is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the stock price was $\\frac{1}{2}$ thousand dollars per week."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f69ffc3-967d-568e-b3f6-17f98cabb1f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.899$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244455} {:answer/id #uuid "623719cf-e4fc-50c5-af6b-82c9236bba68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.736$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245173} {:answer/id #uuid "9b8c808d-a723-5a23-99d4-1fb6cf45cc5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.311$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245689} {:answer/id #uuid "defc4fee-1f26-5c5d-84cf-ab714d860a2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.346$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246291} {:answer/id #uuid "e54a6975-4261-5825-a3df-b1afbd880b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.566$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "623719cf-e4fc-50c5-af6b-82c9236bba68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.736$ muons per microsecond" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245173} :answer-field/id #uuid "6afb29aa-f1d1-5f09-9077-99008241eb9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246734}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c8932d66-35b8-594b-9a87-80583a008ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-112381" :question/problem "The decay rate $M$ of muons in a beam traveling at high speed can be modeled by the function $M(t)=2\\cdot {e}^{-2t},$ where $t$ is the time, in microseconds, since observations started. What will be the decay rate of the muons after $0.5$ microseconds? Round your answer to three decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The function $M(t)$ models the decay rate for the particles $t$ microseconds since observations started.\n\nThus, the decay rate of the muons after $0.5$ microseconds is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(0.5) & =2\\cdot {e}^{-2(0.5)} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {e}^{-1} \\\\  & ≈0.736.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the decay rate of the particles is $0.736$ muons per microsecond."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04171382-cbfa-5f10-92fb-22e5c7a6e6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244346} {:answer/id #uuid "284bf059-1884-5e2d-a5c3-731890221cc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244669} {:answer/id #uuid "51d5b6bd-e195-5c6e-bf88-1a79c021dc21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245038} {:answer/id #uuid "6d228c5d-7d6a-5f80-841c-f0172b125cc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245278} {:answer/id #uuid "7452c71d-92bf-59ad-847f-f7ba52f5ece7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04171382-cbfa-5f10-92fb-22e5c7a6e6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ percent per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244346} :answer-field/id #uuid "4de83a2e-a171-5c7c-a155-600eb37ea0f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246677}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "524d3949-c8de-5ba0-b1ba-ea4e8e41e832" :question/math-academy-id "q-112383" :question/problem "After charging the battery of a PC, the percentage of charge decreases at a rate of $c(t)=100\\cdot {5}^{-0.2t}$ percent per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the battery had completed its charge. What will be the rate of decrease after $5$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the amount of charge after $5$ hours, we have $t=5.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease of the amount of charge after $5$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(5) & =100\\cdot {5}^{-0.2(5)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {5}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{5} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $20$ percent per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f1c6b98-25f8-5e4b-b169-c98a156923ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$162$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245016} {:answer/id #uuid "779d5d52-77eb-5021-9fdb-6949a0551730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$140$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245373} {:answer/id #uuid "811be8e1-8e6b-5190-8d78-5e4b9cd0b31b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$125$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245455} {:answer/id #uuid "c45a009c-113a-5c51-b8a5-aee9dd3c26fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$100$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246059} {:answer/id #uuid "e07a4990-5522-544f-8f86-dacc8fa566a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$120$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e07a4990-5522-544f-8f86-dacc8fa566a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$120$ cars per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246309} :answer-field/id #uuid "78d8582c-8f74-5c8e-a7a1-5a0e9065a5b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246756}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b547e5e1-1e78-5d71-9ff5-a1728add6182" :question/math-academy-id "q-112507" :question/problem "The rate $O$ of the orders a car factory receives can be modeled as $O(t)=100t{e}^{-0.1t}$ cars per day. The rate at which cars are completed can be modeled as $C(t)=50+10sin⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{7}t)$ cars per day. In both cases, $t$ is the time, in days, since the launch of the new model. \n\nWhat is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction $28$ days after the model's launch? Assume that an ordered car goes into construction as soon as the factory receives its order. Round your answer to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of the number of cars under construction at time $t$ is equal to the order rate minus the completion rate, that is,\n\n$$\nO(t)-C(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $t=28,$ the rate of change in the number of cars under construction after $28$ days is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(t)-C(t) & =100(28){e}^{-0.1(28)}-(50+10sin⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{7}(28))) \\\\  & =100(28){e}^{-2.8}-50-10sin⁡(8\\pi ) \\\\  & =100(28){e}^{-2.8}-50 \\\\  & ≈120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the number of cars in construction after $28$ days is $120$ cars per day."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329934 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0400157b-c1a8-53a6-8dcd-8bf81b54d097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$900$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326977} {:answer/id #uuid "35810fd7-3042-5428-8e3d-5d1db0348860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$800$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327400} {:answer/id #uuid "aba393d2-bfb8-5de2-8e57-d8c30468307a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$700$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328420} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f5cc60-bdc1-5422-b8c8-352e070c8ea1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$600$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328901} {:answer/id #uuid "ea12e4e8-1b1a-576e-8cc0-7f6378f95ca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$100\\cdot {2}^{6}$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35810fd7-3042-5428-8e3d-5d1db0348860" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$800$ bacteria per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327400} :answer-field/id #uuid "88a2805a-ae37-515d-a7b8-d5098613d13b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329413}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46629e3f-8b91-52e2-8f67-4405ebbe6de1" :question/math-academy-id "q-48902" :question/problem "The growth rate, $G(t)$, of the number of bacteria in a culture can be modeled by the function $G(t)=100\\cdot {2}^{0.5t}$, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since a sample of bacteria was placed in a Petri dish.  What will be the growth rate of the bacteria after $6$ hours?" :question/worked-solution "The function $G(t)$ models the growth rate for the bacteria $t$ hours since the sample was put in the Petri dish.\n\nThus, the growth rate of the bacteria culture after $6$ hours is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}G(6) & =100\\cdot {2}^{0.5(6)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\  & =100\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =800.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the growth rate of the bacteria is $800$ bacteria per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d986347-5304-5bf8-9489-b5458173cd49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-94$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327049} {:answer/id #uuid "38a1f85b-0932-59c9-8d00-d2afb106da3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-200$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327430} {:answer/id #uuid "5acea6b6-3caf-5eff-af39-aa31ffcec36a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-220$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327729} {:answer/id #uuid "d9489eab-ebee-5d5c-a32b-d59ea30a9b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$420$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328833} {:answer/id #uuid "e22a41b0-6c91-593e-ac0d-e8429be02811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$240$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38a1f85b-0932-59c9-8d00-d2afb106da3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-200$ elephants per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327430} :answer-field/id #uuid "eabd25e6-300b-5d8d-ae1c-f832bb8ce89c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329593}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f24a112-83bc-5dfc-b8eb-4133c86e6e85" :question/math-academy-id "q-48914" :question/problem "The birth rate of a herd of elephants in a region in Africa is modeled by the function  $B(t)=500\\cdot {2}^{0.125t}$ while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t)=400\\cdot {3}^{0.125t}.$ In both cases, $t$ represents the number of years since $1990.$  \n\nWhat was the rate of change of the elephant population in that region in $1998?$" :question/worked-solution "The  rate of change in the number of elephants  $t$ years since $1990$ is equal to the difference between the two given rates, that is\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nAs $1998$ is $8$ years after $1990$, we have $t=8.$  Hence, the  rate of change in the elephant population in that region in $1998$ was \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(8)-D(8) & =500\\cdot {2}^{0.125(8)}-400\\cdot {3}^{0.125(8)} \\\\  & =500\\cdot 2-400\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-200.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the elephant population was $-200$ elephants per year."}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change"}]}
